From: WinBoat
Subject: [PATCH] spirv: size and sample queries on a sampled image

OpImageQuerySizeLod (and the other image queries) take an image; GravityMark's OpenGL shaders (GL_ARB_gl_spirv,
Tellusim's compiler) give them the combined image-sampler, which NVIDIA's and AMD's drivers accept. spirv_to_nir
failed the module, and the WGL driver then read through the missing NIR shader (an access violation in
_mesa_spirv_to_nir). Such a query now queries the sampled image's image.
---
diff --git a/src/compiler/spirv/spirv_to_nir.c b/src/compiler/spirv/spirv_to_nir.c
index 0cf3a3f..bc5e1f8 100644
--- a/src/compiler/spirv/spirv_to_nir.c
+++ b/src/compiler/spirv/spirv_to_nir.c
@@ -6171,6 +6171,12 @@ vtn_handle_body_instruction(struct vtn_builder *b, SpvOp opcode,
    case SpvOpImageQuerySizeLod:
    case SpvOpImageQuerySize: {
       struct vtn_type *image_type = vtn_get_value_type(b, w[3]);
+      /* A query on a sampled image isn't valid SPIR-V, but other drivers take it (GravityMark's OpenGL shaders):
+       * query its image */
+      if (image_type->base_type == vtn_base_type_sampled_image) {
+         vtn_handle_texture(b, opcode, w, count);
+         break;
+      }
       vtn_assert(image_type->base_type == vtn_base_type_image);
       if (glsl_type_is_image(image_type->glsl_image)) {
          vtn_handle_image(b, opcode, w, count);
